      "descriptions": [
        {
          "description": "This dataset includes baseline pathologic, MRI and genomic features of 85 treatment-naive naturally-occurring canine glioma. The data were collected from 5 different veterinary institutions' patient populations. Clinical MRI are available prior to any treatment, and surgical biopsy and/or tissues collected at necropsy are provided as H stained sections. The tumors have been classified with a harmonized classification scheme developed by veterinary and physician neuropathologists. The genomic features were described using whole exome, whole genome, RNAseq and methylation profiling.",
          "descriptionType": "Abstract",
          "lang": null
        }
      ],
